!Name: totalperiodic
!CWithout the block, this is Gosper's "total aperiodic"
!Cpattern (Nov '97), in which every cell in the universe
!Ceventually becomes aperiodic.
!C
!CWith the block, every cell eventually becomes periodic,
!Cbut incredibly slowly. The block remains untouched for
!Cvery roughly 3^63 generations. It deletes the nth glider
!C(and is shifted) at about generation 3^(57.5+5.5n).
!C
!CBill Gosper, 24 Jun '04
!Source: jslife-oversize-20100113
